<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aspurgus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 37/38 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a> · Also known as Tiberius Julius Aspurgus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aspurgus was king of the Bosporan Kingdom in the early 1st century CE, until his death in 37 or 38 CE. A client of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, he received Roman citizenship and founded the line of kings who took the names <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiberius">Tiberius</a> Julius and ruled the kingdom for the next three centuries. He fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scythians">Scythians</a> and the Taurians and secured control of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerch-strait">Cimmerian Bosporus</a>.</p></div>
